  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If the length of a diagonal of a square is \\(a+b,\\) then the area of the square is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\((a+b)^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac12(a+b)^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(a^2+b^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac12(a^2+b^2)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "None of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1951-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(s\\) is the side length and \\(d=a+b\\) is the diagonal, then \\(d=s\\sqrt2.\\) Thus \\[ s^2=\\frac{d^2}{2}=\\frac12(a+b)^2. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Relate the diagonal \\(d\\) of a square to its side \\(s\\)",
        "Since \\(d=s\\sqrt2\\), the area \\(s^2\\) equals \\(\\frac{d^2}{2}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
